    {
      "id": "claim_662ea9b9ec004cd98a9410f3d8b63ddd",
      "statement": "Offer establishment mints the RSA keypair exactly once at the top of generateOfferLink (before the peer exists), creates the RTCPeerConnection with a data channel (ordered:false) using the predicate-resolved ICE server, generates the local offer, then waits for ICE candidates to finish or a 3-second timeout (WAIT_ICE_CANDIDATES_TIMEOUT) before building the offer link; a per-invocation offerBuilt flag claims the build synchronously so the two paths build the link at most once and the timeout fallback can never rotate the key. Regeneration is generation-safe: before minting, generateOfferLink clears the pending ICE-candidate timer, nulls the handlers and closes the old data channel and RTCPeerConnection (unless already closed), and bumps a monotonically increasing offerGeneration token; the timeout fallback re-checks that token at fire time so a stale timer holding the previous generation's public key can never build a link from the new peer's SDP. Synchronous construction/offer-creation failures are caught and toasted instead of leaving the spinner stuck.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/components/OfferPage.svelte#L152-L256",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ff6f6f930900186f478f53c2dd32d20f311af0a2c757aacc336520c2ddc9fa49:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/components/OfferPage.svelte#L68-L90",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a666cad158278ec91e5f57c3adf05cf7705d1210721d7094ffb815818a8f59a5:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/offer-peer-lifecycle.test.mjs",
          "version": "repo-file-v1:sha256:cd6275d13925307ac229f584cb5705b85625daa8e4a3ace0ba70898685d48743"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_168fa874ca494eb0b49c143450d46e27",
      "statement": "The answer peer decodes the attacker-controllable `s` URL param via sdpDecode (which throws synchronously on empty, invalid-base64, or non-SDP input) inside a try/catch that surfaces an 'Invalid SDP in link' toast instead of crashing the page during load (PR #45); the setOfferSDP promise is kept and awaited before createAnswer with a signalingState === 'have-remote-offer' check, so a rejected setRemoteDescription flips offerFailed and the UI renders an error state ('offer in the link is invalid') instead of the spinner spinning forever; it then awaits the validated p-param key import (a malformed key downgrades the session to plaintext) and produces the answer code sdpEncode(answerSdp) + '|' + base64(RSA public key) with the same 3-second ICE candidate timeout fallback.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/components/ReceivePage.svelte#L138-L178",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ae357d9454cce157c733521cb403de2034be521aba815babde32f2e006098306:"
        },
