    {
      "id": "claim_c2c408a79a5f495fa0bf3c5b1efcccdb",
      "statement": "All data-channel traffic is proto3-framed Message bytes: a file id plus exactly one of metaData (name, size, type, encrypted AES key), chunk (file body slice), or receiveEvent (receiver control event); there is no ad-hoc text protocol on the channel.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/proto/message.proto#L1-L31",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9f8c0ab1d2ddf1af4c03d3743789407e5f7307442c33e3dfe52c728531974356:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_311d6dea83ac47ecbb8e7a3de45ee72a",
      "statement": "Both pages dispatch incoming data-channel messages with the same oneof switch (metaData routes to Receiver.onMetaData, chunk to Receiver.onChunkData, receiveEvent to Sender.onReceiveEvent), with Message.decode on the peer-controlled bytes wrapped in try/catch on both pages so a malformed/truncated protobuf frame drops the frame and toasts 'Invalid message from peer' instead of crashing the page uncaught (PR #46).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/components/OfferPage.svelte#L107-L127",
